{"arc_id":"PU_1993_HW_3DO","subject":"3DO","arc_type":"EXPECTATION_TO_SKEPTICISM_TO_HANDS_ON_REASSESSMENT","statement":"Across the five issues, 3DO moves from extraordinary future-facing claims, through explicit skepticism about demonstrations and hype, to a real Netherlands hands-on encounter that causes PU to revise its earlier caution. This is a synthesis inference, not a single contemporaneous PU verdict.","epistemic_status":"INFERENCE_FROM_CHRONOLOGICAL_PRIMARY_EVIDENCE","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_001","pdf_page":10,"layer":"BEST_MACHINE_TRANSCRIPT_BY_PAGE","source_file":"auth/PU1/BLACKPAPER_PU_001_COMPLETE_ARCHIVE_v2/raw_text/PU_001_BEST_MACHINE_TRANSCRIPT_BY_PAGE.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_001","pdf_page":11,"layer":"BEST_MACHINE_TRANSCRIPT_BY_PAGE","source_file":"auth/PU1/BLACKPAPER_PU_001_COMPLETE_ARCHIVE_v2/raw_text/PU_001_BEST_MACHINE_TRANSCRIPT_BY_PAGE.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_pages":[16],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_002_KNOW_007","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_pages":[45],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_003_KNOW_025","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_pages":[13],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_005_KNOW_009","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_pages":[13],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_005_KNOW_010","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null}]}
{"arc_id":"PU_1993_HW_JAGUAR","subject":"Atari Jaguar","arc_type":"RUMOR_TO_SPEC_ERROR_TO_CORRECTION_TO_HANDS_ON","statement":"Jaguar begins as a 64-bit rumor/report, is described in issue 2 with an onboard double-speed compact disc, is challenged by a reader in issue 3 and reframed as cartridge hardware with optional CD expansion, then becomes a confirmed hands-on machine in issue 5.","epistemic_status":"MIXED_DIRECT_FACT_AND_CROSS_ISSUE_SYNTHESIS","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_001","pdf_page":11,"layer":"BEST_MACHINE_TRANSCRIPT_BY_PAGE","source_file":"auth/PU1/BLACKPAPER_PU_001_COMPLETE_ARCHIVE_v2/raw_text/PU_001_BEST_MACHINE_TRANSCRIPT_BY_PAGE.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_pages":[16],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_002_KNOW_009","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_page":8,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":"reader correction/challenge"},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_pages":[14],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_003_KNOW_010","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_pages":[15],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_005_KNOW_017","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_pages":[15],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_005_KNOW_018","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null}]}
{"arc_id":"PU_1993_HW_VR","subject":"Virtual Reality","arc_type":"CONTESTED_FUTURE_PREDICTION","statement":"The corpus does not contain one unified PU position on VR. Issue 2 contains both near-term Sega VR expectation and a positive long-term prediction after a primitive demo; issue 3 prints Laurens Stolker rejecting VR; issue 4 prints Edward Laauwen predicting VR games as the future. These voices must remain distinct.","epistemic_status":"DIRECTLY_OBSERVED_CONTRADICTION_OF_VOICES","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_pages":[17],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_002_KNOW_010","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_pages":[23],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_002_KNOW_023","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_pages":[45],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_003_KNOW_025","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_004","pdf_pages":[65],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_004_KNOW_037","source_file":"PU4/PU_004_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_004_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null}]}
